{
  "info": {
    "name": "Paiflow API v1",
    "description": "Execute a deployed swapper flow and poll its events. Fill in the collection variables `deploymentId`, `apiToken` (minted by the deployment's owner in the API access panel), `from` and `amount`.\n\nThe API never signs. Run **Prepare execute**, sign the `unsignedXdr` variable it stores with the `from` key on your side (`stellar tx sign --sign-with-key S… --network testnet`), paste the result into `signedXdr`, then run **Submit execute**. Guide: docs/api/README.md in the repository.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{apiToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://paiflow.xyz"
    },
    {
      "key": "deploymentId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "apiToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "from",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "amount",
      "value": "10000000"
    },
    {
      "key": "unsignedXdr",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "signedXdr",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "txHash",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "cursor",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "OpenAPI document",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/openapi.json",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "openapi.json"]
        },
        "description": "Public; no token. Returned as the bare document, without the `data` envelope. Rate limit: 60 requests per 60 seconds per client IP."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('returns the OpenAPI document', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().openapi).to.match(/^3\\.1/);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/openapi.json",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "openapi.json"]
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"openapi\": \"3.1.0\",\n  \"info\": {\n    \"title\": \"Paiflow API v1\"\n  },\n  \"…\": \"…\"\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Prepare execute",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": \"{{amount}}\",\n  \"from\": \"{{from}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "Prepare the deposit that executes a swapper flow. `from` must be a funded account on this network: it pays the deposit and the fee, and signs the envelope. The flow's payout recipient must hold a trustline for the asset it receives; a missing trustline reverts the whole pipeline.\n\nThe flow runs through its deposit trigger; the swapper executes as the next pipeline step. Sign the returned `xdr` with the `from` key using `networkPassphrase`, before `expiresAt`, and post it to `execute/submit`. Only swapper flows can be executed.\n\nRate limit: 30 requests per 60 seconds per token."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('returns an unsigned envelope', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  const { data } = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(data.xdr).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('unsignedXdr', data.xdr);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 OK",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": \"{{amount}}\",\n  \"from\": \"{{from}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"xdr\": \"AAAAAgAAAADYXPYQYOTpvJD2BAs8oB9ej3hbUuLzjbut2WPA6+L0OQAB6IQADc4pAAAAAQAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABmxy2kAAAAAAAAAAEAAAAAAAAAGAAAAAAAAAAB…(truncated)\",\n    \"networkPassphrase\": \"Test SDF Network ; September 2015\",\n    \"network\": \"testnet\",\n    \"expiresAt\": \"2026-09-15T09:03:00.000Z\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "401 Unauthorized",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": \"{{amount}}\",\n  \"from\": \"{{from}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "status": "Unauthorized",
          "code": 401,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\",\n    \"message\": \"A valid API token for this deployment is required\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "422 Validation",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": \"{{amount}}\",\n  \"from\": \"{{from}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "status": "Unprocessable Entity",
          "code": 422,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"VALIDATION\",\n    \"message\": \"Invalid input\",\n    \"fields\": {\n      \"amount\": [\n        \"Must be a whole number of stroops\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Submit execute",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute/submit",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute", "submit"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"signedXdr\": \"{{signedXdr}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "Submit a signed deposit that executes a swapper flow.\n\nThe envelope must be the one `execute` returned, signed by `from`: anything but a single `deposit` call on this flow's trigger contract is refused with `VALIDATION`, as is a fee-bump envelope.\n\nIdempotent on the envelope hash: submitting the same `signedXdr` again never sends a second transaction, it reports the one already on the network. That is also how to check a `PENDING` result. A transaction that reached the network and failed is a `200` with `status: FAILED` and an `error`, not an HTTP error.\n\nRate limit: 30 requests per 60 seconds per token."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('reports the outcome', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  const { data } = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(['SUCCESS', 'PENDING', 'FAILED']).to.include(data.status);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('txHash', data.txHash);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 SUCCESS",
          "originalRequest": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/execute/submit",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "deployments", "{{deploymentId}}", "execute", "submit"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"signedXdr\": \"{{signedXdr}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "body": "{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"txHash\": \"94be52e8a937b6ddcb85da7cd917f97d412753e5e3ca47ea48b252a264b2278d\",\n    \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\n    \"ledger\": 1842917\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "200 PENDING",
          "originalRequest": {
